ek 12 Anger Index: Indiana dropped how many spots?!","description":"Ranking the teams that should be most upset with the latest CFP rankings.","published":"2026-11-25T13:05:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50582371/cfp-ranking-2026-anger-index-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on the College Football Playoff bubble after committee's fourth ranking?","description":"A conference-by-conference look at which teams are contending for the playoff, who's close and who's out.","published":"2026-11-25T13:04:11.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575185/cfp-playoff-2026-bubble-watch-week-fourth-ranking","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Why UTEP-NIU is 2026's most unglamorous Game of the Century","description":"The Week 13 game will mark the first time since at least 2000 that two teams that are winless against FBS opponents will meet in their final week of the regular season.","published":"2026-11-25T01:19:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50587546/utep-niu-college-football-game-century","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana falls from 12-team field in 4th CFP rankings; Horns, Vols leap Bama","description":"Defending champ Indiana fell six spots to No. 14, while Alabama was leaped by Texas and Tennessee and fell out of the top five in the latest CFP rankings Tuesday night.","published":"2026-11-25T07:42:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50588082/indiana-top-12-cfp-rankings-texas-tennessee-leap-alabama","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on the move? CFP committee's fourth top 25 and bracket of 2026","description":"A look at the new bracket based on the College Football Playoff committee's fourth set of rankings.","published":"2026-11-25T02:02:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584328/cfp-2026-fourth-committee-top-25-bracket","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5136784/francis-brewu","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Brewu"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Francis Brewu","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Brewu","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:30Z","intro":"Francis Brewu (born January 17, 2006) is an American college football defensive tackle for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish. He previously played for the Pittsburgh Panthers.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In January 2024, Brewu enrolled early at Pittsburgh. He quickly impressed during spring camp due to his size and technique and was moved off of the scout team. He was also named the strongest player on the team by his teammates. Prior to the 2024 season, Brewu was named number 77 on Bruce Feldman’s Freaks List. During the season he played in 12 games with one start and totaled 15 tackles, three tackles for loss and 1.5 sacks. He was also named to the Pro Football Focus (PFF) All-Freshman Team at the end of the season. In December 2024, Brewu announced he would return to the Panthers for 2025. On August 4, 2025, Brewu was again named to Feldman's Freaks List, this time at number 24. In 2025 Brewu started 12 games for the Panthers in which he led all Pitt interior defensive linemen in tackles. Due to his performance, Brewu gained recognition as an Honorable Mention All-ACC selection. On January 6, 2026, Brewu entered the transfer portal, and chose to transfer to the Notre Dame Fighting Irish on January 13. On August 10, 2026, Brewu was named to Bruce Feldman’s Freaks List for the third consecutive season."}]}}